#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0116 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "FRESH (shape ADAPTED-FROM fda/FDA-SD0072-invalid-SUPPAE.cdt, re-cut SUPPAE->CO). Row 1: RDOMAIN=BW is a registered study dataset -> clean. Rows 2 and 3: RDOMAIN=ZZ names no study dataset -> BOTH fire, PER RECORD. *** AUTHORED ON THE stage-r FALLBACK, NOT THE PER-SUBJECT PIN. *** M3-SEND-T2-K3-01 listed this scenario as an SD1316-F3 D9 predicted red, gating on the primary being CO rather than DM; but the ruling's own corrected test is on the membership LEFT OPERAND, which here is RDOMAIN - a domain abbreviation, named explicitly in the M2 false-positive list. CDISC-SEND-0116 is therefore NOT in the SD1316-F3 population, gets no Grouping block, and reports per record. This file is the instruction's documented one-edit fallback: count 2 with the two per-record at-pins."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=2 RDOMAIN=ZZ
#expectViolationAt row=3 RDOMAIN=ZZ
dataset CO class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO | BW | 001 | 1 | Comment on body weight
S1 | CO | ZZ | 002 | 1 | First bad reference
S1 | CO | ZZ | 002 | 2 | Second bad reference
---

dataset BW label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col BWTESTCD type=Char label="Body Weight Test Short Name"
col BWORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | BW | 250
---
